; Part of ferrum. MIT licence, see ferrum/LICENSE.
; Common checks for the rotary A probe macros (probe_a_*):
; o<ferrum_rotary_ready> call [need xy clearance]. Runs
; o<ferrum_probe_ready> (probe loaded, settings usable, G40, machine
; units, no G52/G92, no rotation), then refuses a Z clearance #3021 under
; 10 mm and, when the argument is 1, an XY clearance #3019 under 5 mm (both
; converted to machine units), and a tip with no effective radius
; (#5410/2 - #3032). Sets #<_ferrum_mm> to one
; millimetre in machine units for the callers' own small distances. No
; motion.
o<ferrum_rotary_ready> sub
o<ferrum_probe_ready> call
o100 if [#<_metric_machine> EQ 1]
    #<_ferrum_mm> = 1
o100 else
    #<_ferrum_mm> = [1 / 25.4]
o100 endif
o105 if [#3021 LT [10 * #<_ferrum_mm>]]
    (ABORT, Rotary probing requires Z clearance #3021 of at least 10 mm)
o105 endif
o106 if [[#1 EQ 1] AND [#3019 LT [5 * #<_ferrum_mm>]]]
    (ABORT, Rotary probing requires XY clearance #3019 of at least 5 mm)
o106 endif
o108 if [[[#5410 / 2] - #3032] LE 0]
    (ABORT, Effective probe tip radius must be positive)
o108 endif
o<ferrum_rotary_ready> endsub
M2
